NOT ADDITIVE. The marginals cannot be mixed across knobs, so a
joint table built from them would be fiction. Either run the
full 6x4 grid (l220_grid.sh, ~66 min) or restrict the joint
search to the (k, R) pairs actually measured.

Note the weighted error column: a small weighted error with many
per-case mismatches means the interaction exists but is not
weighted where it matters -- that is a REASON TO MEASURE the
chosen pair, not a licence to mix.
